  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There have been many times where I have either forgotten what mode my camera is on or have just forgotten to switch it before hand. This is especially prevalent when recording clips. It is very frustrating to find out an entire clip is unusable because I forgot to swap to stream mode or accidentally toggled it without realizing. I think a good solution for this would be to just put an obvious indicator somewhere on the camera for what mode it is in. It could be, for instance, a red light in a corner of the camera to show streamer mode is on, or maybe having the different symbols appear in the corner. It could even be as simple as having lettering above the camera saying \"Stream\" or \"Photo\". There could be an additional setting under the camera mode to disable this if someone doesn't want it as well.\n\nWhile there is an indicator already on the camera, I do not feel it is obvious enough. Especially if you are in VR, it can be very easy to not even glance at the current one. So I think a more obvious indicator would be more beneficial",
